"title":"Upstart Holdings, Inc. Updates Earnings Guidance for the Full Year 2026","src":"www.marketscreener.com","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxNNzc0OG9oMG5JVlIzLUVhYXNNZlQxVTQtQWo0Wk5qcld1T21MeTYtTzRFaUxsZlZqNVBkS28wRi1yTVNCeHNyT1V3cTdCS0ZDRndJQ0tqRVpRcEFEVjJ0RlpaSGR4RVN5UFJOVGZCUGIwSlVTMk9QX1NfRVliU2NacWQ2cHc2dXFuNl9ZYU81N2Vsel9NZzI1VW96V3FzRl9hd0ZZUTN2aUhpdDFuc2NMb0ZOOGt2dnk4OGVnd1BqTQ?oc=5","date":"2026-11-03","zh":"Upstart Holdings, Inc. 更新 2026 年全年獲利指引"},{"title":"Upstart Shares Are Retreating Tuesday: What's Happening? (CORRECTED)","src":"Benzinga","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxOb1ZKRUg2SF9SWFAxbmk5alp5ZlNmTGhDQ2d0U00wbnIyZ2JSTlczY3NSYnBwR2xoWjFvS3V0V3Y5SkdOZXByX2tUaW9XX2l5Y05yYTcyNmk2WmRIbnhxUkgzV3B4SFJQWlY4aXNEUkVaYUpZTXNzMU9OUnJueklReHBHeFRiRjJtODQwOG0wN3ktRmJrbVNrRDUwWC1ZdGxvOWltLWpyVV8wMFpLWS1vZVJVaW4?oc=5","date":"2026-11-03","zh":"新貴股價週二回落：發生了什麼事？ （已更正）"},{"title":"Upstart (UPST) Stock Looks About Right On Expanded Auto Lending Deal","src":"Simply Wall St","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-10-27","zh":"Upstart (UPST) 股票看起來與擴大汽車貸款交易有關"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":6},{"name":"分析師評等","count":2},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-10","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1647639/000164763926000027/upst-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Upstart is the leading artificial intelligence (\"AI\") lending marketplace. We aim to radically reduce the cost and complexity of borrowing for all Americans by using our proprietary AI models to remake the entire lending process. Founded in 2012, Upstart's marketplace supports unsecured and secured credit products, such as personal loans, auto loans, and home equity lines of credit (\"HELOCs\"). Long-term, our vision is to become the always-on, everything-store for credit, where we can automatically approve borrowers at the right prices – instantly and effortlessly.","zh":null},{"en":"We're dedicated to providing the best rates and the best process to all consumers. Throughout history, affordable credit has been central to unlocking mobility and opportunity. The FICO score was invented in 1989 and remains the standard for determining who is approved for credit and at what interest rate. While FICO is rarely the only input in a lending decision, most lenders use simple rules-based systems that consider only a limited number of variables. Unfortunately, because these legacy credit systems fail to accurately identify and quantify risk, millions of creditworthy individuals are left out of the system, and millions more pay too much to borrow money.","zh":null},{"en":"Our platform applies AI to more accurately quantify the true risk of a loan, a capability we refer to as \"risk separation.\" This differentiated approach to underwriting has generally led to higher approvals and lower interest rates relative to traditional lending practices, with more predictable returns to our capital partners including banks and credit unions (collectively our \"lending partners\") and institutional investors. With this as the foundation, we've added layers of automation, macroeconomic calibration, and personalization that can support increasing scale and greater business resilience over time.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"Consumer lending is a vast and competitive market, and we compete in varying degrees with all other sources of unsecured and secured consumer credit, including banks, non-bank lenders (including retail-based lenders), and other financial technology lending platforms. Because personal loans often serve as a replacement for credit cards, we also compete with the convenience and ubiquity that credit cards represent.","zh":null},{"en":"On the lending partnership side, we compete with a variety of technology companies that aim to help lenders with the digital transformation of their business, particularly with respect to all-digital lending. This includes new products from legacy lending technology providers as well as newer companies focused entirely on lending software infrastructure for lenders. We may also face competition from lenders or companies that have not previously competed in the consumer lending market, including companies with large and experienced machine learning teams and access to vast amounts of consumer-related information that could be used in the development of their own credit risk models.","zh":null}],"segments":{"prod":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Origination Fees","val":7600000,"zh":"Origination Fees"},{"name":"Subscription Fee","val":4700000,"zh":"Subscription Fee"}],"total":1043857000}},"peers":["AFRM","SOFI","U","TTD","CVNA"]}}